>El-Deiry</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Non-invasive fluorescence imaging of cell death in fresh human colon epithelia treated with 5-Fluorouracil, CPT-11 and&#x0002f;or TRAIL</article-title><source>Cancer Biol Ther</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>937</fpage><lpage>942</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Biol Ther||4|937||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16251801</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fiorucci</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mencarelli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Palazzetti</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Del</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Morelli</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ignarro</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An NO derivative of ursodeoxycholic acid protects against Fas-mediated liver injury by inhibiting caspase activity</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>2652</fpage><lpage>2657</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Proc Natl Acad Sci USA||98|2652||bib9|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galligan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Longley</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>McEwan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>McLaughlin</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnston</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chemotherapy and TRAIL-mediated colon cancer cell death: the roles of p53, TRAIL receptors, and c-FLIP</article-title><source>Mol Cancer Ther</source><year>2005</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>2026</fpage><lpage>2036</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Mol Cancer Ther||4|2026||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16373718</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>PR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosella</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mariadason</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rickard</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Byron</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Barkla</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Colonic epithelial cell activation and the paradoxical effects of butyrate</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>1999</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>539</fpage><lpage>544</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Carcinogenesis||20|539||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10223179</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gliniak</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Le</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tumor necrosis factor-related apoptosis-inducing ligand's antitumor activity <italic>in vivo</italic> is enhanced by the chemotherapeutic agent CPT-11</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>6153</fpage><lpage>6158</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||59|6153||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10626806</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grosch</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tegeder</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Niederberger</surnam